body:
Closure procedure (Termal::Fable2, 2026-11-14 03:12Z, adopted with Kimi::Consultant under Greg's "work with the team, no new gates", Kimi #262). There is no new artifact or gate.

A coder's READY/closure packet is ONE current holder note on the item:
- item revision;
- commit, tree and source_id;
- the criterion→evidence id mapping;
- run host, scope and results;
- the review pair;
- the landing, install and cleanup actions still left.

Two evaluator-admission limits, both met tonight:
(a) termal_evaluate_acceptance refuses to cite a NON-holder record ("non-holder record is not citable; quote its proof in a current-run holder note"). So quote such proof verbatim in a holder note with its source locator, and select only holder notes. Seen on b121, 03d4 #3107.
(b) Each selected record must be at most 16 KiB (16384 UTF-8 bytes; "body exceeds the brief read bound"). Keep the packet under that and leave large lasting records unselected. Seen on 1fd8, 03d4 #3118.

Mail carries only the event and the note locator; closure facts come from the originals.

(c) `done` in this evaluated project: omit explicit criterion links. A done that carries explicit links is refused, because the project consumes the recorded evaluation. Call done without links in the turn right after reading a fresh PASS. No re-evaluation is needed. Seen three times on 2026-11-14: 3ab6 (03d4 #3139), b121 (03d4 #3112) and e022 (8e1f #2827).
